//
// Item inspect panel: a live 3D ItemPreviewWidget, a rotate-left and a rotate-right button and a
// close button. The script gives the widget an item, turns the model with SetModelOrientation and
// cleans up when the panel closes.
//
// How the layout is built (rules measured on a live client, see references/gui-layouts.md):
//  - The priority limit. An ItemPreviewWidget drew nothing, with no error and no log line, when its
//    priority or an ancestor's was 300 or more (256 and lower drew; the ancestor half of that rule
//    is still being re-measured, see section 13 of references/gui-layouts.md). So this root is
//    priority 200 and every child is lower. Do not give this root the 998 or 999 that
//    menu_filter_list.layout gives its modal root, and check the whole chain if you embed this
//    panel in another layout.
//  - The preview has ignorepointer 1, as 49 of the 52 vanilla previews do: the buttons turn the
//    model. Drag-to-rotate would need a widget that takes the mouse (OnMouseButtonDown) instead.
//  - The root is centered with halign and valign center_ref plus exact position 0 0, and every
//    size is in layout units (1 unit is 1 px at 1080 rows, H / 1080 px on a taller screen).
//  - Each button is style Empty with an opaque Bg child and a caption child TextWidget, all of
//    them ignorepointer 1, exactly as in menu_filter_list.layout. userID tells the buttons apart.
//
// Script companion (client side, for example 5_Mission/MyMod/MyModItemPreview.c). The load path
// starts at the mod's own pbo prefix:
